## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | memory/note/n_1030_8dda.md | 🚨 blocking pr re tracks the gitignored project memory path memory scope violation this pr adds two new tracked files memory note n 1030 8dda md and memory note n 1030 a0cf md — raw memory add agent session artifacts accesscount importance frontmatter agent wiki links — under the memory path the repo deliberately closed to git in gh 2185 gitignore gitignore 229 236 gh 2185 memory left git too — the project memory store consolidated into fah memory local only covered by the fah rules above the root copy is ignored so the old path can never re track notes memory verified on this branch git ls tree origin main memory → empty nothing under memory is tracked on main the merge base is the gh 2185 hygiene commit itself both files are tracked only on ai gh 2194 i e force added through an ignore rule whose stated purpose is the old path can never re track notes git check ignore memory note new md → matches gitignore 236 memory agents md memory footnote project scope is fah memory note since gh 2185 — local only not committed the pr description says site markup one new test only — the notes are unacknowledged scope the wip auto save sweep class the gitignore comment right above warns about this is exactly the two homes divergence gh 2185 just eliminated tracked logs generated dumps purged memory store consolidated to one home the ticket s fix is landing page markup guard test so these files are scope creep beyond it fix untrack both files without deleting them locally bash git rm cached memory note n 1030 8dda md memory note n 1030 a0cf md if either note has lasting value it belongs in fah memory local via memory add or as durable documentation under docs — not in a tracked memory directory |
| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | test/site/landing_deep_links_test.dart | 💡 suggestion the guard s regex is not the same extraction contract as the ci probe it mirrors the doc comment lines 32 34 claims same extraction contract as scripts assert release assets sh landing but the regex differs from the script s extractor on two axes the script assert release assets sh landing mode uses bash url class printf t urls grep oe https url class page grep e releases latest download i e scheme https and a class that stops at both quote types and this test matches https only and stops at only — so a future landing page edit that introduces an http …releases latest download … link or a single quoted url would pass this offline guard and still red the tag train probe hours later — precisely the rot class gh 2194 the guard exists to catch offline verified against the current page both extractors agree only … releases latest download fa extension zip which is in the required set so this is latent — but the parity claim should be exact or the narrowing documented suggested fix keeps the parity true dart final deeplinks regexp https t releases latest download t allmatches index map m m group 0 toset or keep https and drop the same extraction contract sentence stating the deliberate narrowing instead — same for the script s tr d space vs the test s trim equivalent under the one name per line required set contract |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

